        <div class="fc-question">Will the United States conduct new airstrikes or missile strikes on internationally recognized Iranian territory after October 6 and before December 5, 2026?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">55%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-12-05</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Trump told aides he expects to resume bombing Iran in November after midterms (November 3) if no deal. The October 3 Camp David session — Vance, Rubio, Hegseth, Witkoff, Ratcliffe, and Caine meeting unannounced — structurally mirrors the June 2025 session held days before the US-Israeli air campaign commenced; at least one participant said decisions were reached. Iran&#8217;s October 5 &#8220;meaningless&#8221; declaration closes the diplomatic off-ramp. Trump publicly stated Iran decision &#8220;coming imminently, easy way or hard way.&#8221; Offset by optionality if mediator breakthrough materializes before midterms.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if CENTCOM, Pentagon, White House, or official US spokesperson confirms airstrikes or missile strikes on targets inside internationally recognized Iranian territory after October 6 and before December 5, 2026. US strikes in Yemen, Iraq, Syria, or against Iranian-affiliated non-state actors outside Iran: NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM press releases, DoD statements, White House readouts (primary); Reuters, AP, AFP, NYT, WaPo preponderance as fallback for unacknowledged operations.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Strikes by Israel with acknowledged US targeting/weapons support but not direct US-launched ordnance: NO. Covert operations without official acknowledgment: resolve on preponderance of TIER1 reporting from ≥3 credentialed wire services or major US newspapers by December 10.</dd>
