      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (30%):</strong> No new US strikes and no confirmed Iran-US diplomatic session materializes; Hormuz remains effectively closed, economic pressure intensifies on both sides, and the conflict enters a frozen-escalatory equilibrium without resolution.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (15%):</strong> No new US strikes and a confirmed Iran-US indirect session occurs before October 20 (F2, p=0.24) or a formal diplomatic proposal emerges from the Guterres Pakistan channel (F1, p=0.14), reopening a negotiating track that reduces resumed-bombing probability. [Derivation: (1&#8722;0.55)&#215;[1&#8722;(0.86&#215;0.76)]&#8776;15%]</p>
